title: Implement c2c host binding and selected-message ack transport
updated_at: "2026-10-16T13:27:32Z"
---
Research: .collab/research/2026-10-16-t3-code-c2c-support.md and live receipt JSON. Quality: preserve existing codebase architecture; small typed interfaces; meaningful regression and failure tests; no mock-only delivery claims; no whole-tree refactor; independent review/fix loop before merge. Decisions and evidence must be appended through bl. Implement canonical OCaml support needed by T3 to bind stable host-managed identity, inspect message envelopes and acknowledge only selected durably accepted IDs. Existing proven primitives should be reused. Regression tests cover malformed/untrusted IDs, concurrent arrival, repeat ack, namespace isolation, DND/flags, restart, and existing clients. Do not start or inject into a provider behind T3.

Lane: c2c host transport and durable source metadata; separate worktree with parent-owned backlog. Native c2c hook suppression reuses C2C_NO_AUTO_REGISTER=1. Tests run on x-p35; no local suites. Provider source writes local/remote/unknown explicitly, legacy unknown; no alias-based wake proof.

Review decision: bounded host peek pages (default/max 64 and <=4MiB serialized message budget) prevent unbounded subprocess replies. Oversized UTF-8 bodies return metadata-only content:null/content_omitted_reason:oversized/content_bytes, allowing durable unsupported acceptance and selective ack without truncation. Include has_more and dnd_until so T3 drains pages and schedules timed-DND expiry without polling.

Lane refinement: native-consumer exclusion is a required host transport primitive, so this c2c lane will add C2C_MCP_DISABLED=1 before its final gate. Disabled native MCP must stay protocol-valid while advertising no tools and rejecting direct tool calls, and must skip startup registration, draining, room join, schedulers/notifications. CLI host commands remain available. T3 setup in E2.T003 will set this per-provider-process flag plus hook/channel suppression. This avoids provider-specific installed-config mutation and prevents arbitrary named native c2c servers consuming T3-owned inboxes.